Ways the change could fail a criterion (advisory — no verdict depends on these):

  record-failure-test-failure-matrix
    [missing_case] record-failure-test-failure-matrix/missing-unusable-shape-entry
      A pair answered in a non-verdict shape is still dropped from the returned matrix instead of being recorded as an unjudged result with its reason.
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#3
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#4
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#5
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#6
    [wrong_output_shape] record-failure-test-failure-matrix/lenient-parser-misreads-strict-shapes
      The lenient parse path can accept a strict verdict shape but then treat a missing reason as `None` or an empty string in a way that collapses distinct answer shapes, so the recorded yes/no matrix loses the failure-mode distinction the review is supposed to preserve.
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#2
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#4
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#5

  pair-failure-reason-observable
    [missing_case] pair-failure-reason-observable/failing-pair-without-reason-marked-unjudged
      A pair that is actually failing but comes back with no reason is diverted into `unjudged` instead of being recorded as a failing verdict with its pair identity and reason.
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#4
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#5
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#6
    [wrong_output_shape] pair-failure-reason-observable/failing-pair-reason-lost-when-parsed-leniently
      The lenient parse path stores `reason` as `None` or strips it away for a failing entry, so the recorded verdict no longer includes the short reason even though the pair is marked failing.
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#2
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#4
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#5

  pair-not-fail-no-reason-and-nothing-else
    [wrong_output_shape] pair-not-fail-no-reason-and-nothing-else/surviving-entry-still-carries-reason
      A verdict for a non-failing pair can still be emitted with a reason field present, because the lenient parser accepts `reason=None` and `_ask` only strips it into `reason = (judged.reason or "").strip()` before deciding what to record.
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#2
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#4
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#5
    [missing_case] pair-not-fail-no-reason-and-nothing-else/nonfailing-entry-dropped-as-unjudged
      A pair that would not fail but is returned in the lenient shape with `fails=False` and no reason is not added to `answered`, so the caller records it as `UNANSWERED` instead of as a recorded non-failing verdict.
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#4
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#5
      src/acceptance/defects/pair_mapping.py#6

